What it does: Movement can occur in x and y direction. Currently no jumping implemented. Walking animation as well as making sure player doesn't stop mid walking animation and freeze on that frame when no movement key is selected. Player can teleport via mouse click, with position centered on the cursor and a teleport animation playing.
How AI was used: AI was used in generous amounts to find more optimal ways to write code, debug, and write the XML file so that I didn't have to constantly make tweaks or count pixel count. Overall very helpful! Also was able to understand what it was doing towards, would recommend not using it early on the development process though.
For sources: Google gemini was used as well as the Monogame 2D project template/tutorial. That is exclusively where code wsas taken from or strategies were implemented from. Monogame or AI. Also the sprite sheet was taken from the website displayed on screen when playing the game, however this is a VERY sketchy website. I genuinely don't know why the sprite sheet is on that website and why it is the best quality sprite sheet I could find, but ultimately I wasn't using the website for anything else.
GITHUB REPO: (Very new to source control, also was only a one person project so didn't utilize best practices or comments when committing: https://github.com/AdamRehan/CSE-3902--Video-Game-)